  "context": {
    "text": "How this run is scored & why 32k\u2013128k drop on a 16k KV server: Each answer is graded deterministically against ground-truth clinical criteria (rubric_weighted_score), target FHIR resourceUuid citation recall (required_uuid_recall), and sentence-level [N] claim-to-UUID entailment (atomic_entailment_rate). On the shared UW CIRG L4 GPU (24 GB VRAM), Ollama defaults to a fixed num_ctx = 16,384 KV window (usage.prompt_tokens = 16,387): when a 32k, 64k, or 128k chart exceeds 16,384 tokens without a dynamic num_ctx override, Ollama silently left-truncates the beginning of the prompt\u2014clipping top-of-chart active allergies, active conditions, active medications, and 2025\u20132026 admissions ([1]\u2013[349]) and leaving only older 2022\u20132023 records ([350]+). Med Agent Hub (+KB & Graph) retains 53.0\u201353.8/100 at 32k\u2013128k (vs. 20.4\u201321.2 Raw) because Stage 2 KB findings and the ClinicalEntityGraph are appended at the bottom of the prompt inside the surviving 16,384-token KV tail.",
